[{:db/id 17592186162115 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" "question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" "question-a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad" "question-953449db-a540-520d-adff-108b01b9d257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161681 :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta) = 3\\ln\\theta + 4\\ln(1-\\theta),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta.$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{\\theta -1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\theta }+\\frac{4}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3(\\theta -1)+4\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 3(\\theta -1)+4\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 7\\theta -3 & =0 \\\\ 7\\theta  & =3 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} =  \\dfrac{3}{7}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162116 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d834043c-817d-50e2-98ca-784bf169d161" "question-d69af2de-f48e-5047-98b1-6977b8b554d5" "question-54d12174-c052-5371-9f75-2200e071a1fb" "question-31869bf1-d8be-5a63-a737-e3c2335ce819" "question-4510ff72-383e-5b2d-aa54-f6d78aa69e2d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161682 :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent normal random variables $X_i\\sim N(\\theta,1)$ is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta) = -6\\ln(2\\pi)-8.4 + 12.1\\, \\! \\theta - 6\\ \\! \\theta^2,\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,}$ for this sample? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta.$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-8.4+12.1\\,\\,\\theta -6\\text{ }\\,{\\theta }^{2}) \\\\  & =12.1-12\\text{ }\\,\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12.1-12\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 12\\text{ }\\,\\theta  & =12.1 \\\\ \\theta  & ≈1.008\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta$ is $\\widehat{\\,\\theta\\,} \\approx 1.008,$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162395 :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\theta }+\\frac{1}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\theta }+\\frac{1}{\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\theta }+\\frac{1}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5(\\theta -1)+\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 5(\\theta -1)+\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 6\\theta -5 & =0 \\\\ 6\\theta  & =5 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159572 :answer-field/correct 17592186159574 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/id #uuid "8cb508aa-a9ee-56b2-be2a-f7d71a96d61c" :question/math-academy-id "q-159963" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{\\theta }+\\frac{12}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8(\\theta -1)+12\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 8(\\theta -1)+12\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 20\\theta -8 & =0 \\\\ 20\\theta  & =8 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{2}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f74069f-b86f-503f-a061-d9ec00b1c8bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa" "answer-d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8" "answer-4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786" "answer-694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" "answer-ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa" :answer/id #uuid "f262d641-ad09-5541-a1b9-b14c2d786ffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8" :answer/id #uuid "d2d0294e-3e9f-5fe9-9082-3c690994a0b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786" :answer/id #uuid "4162e3d9-b07a-5986-95b7-183bc014b786" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" :answer/id #uuid "694a6d77-b1f1-591c-bc99-15a19344806a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00" :answer/id #uuid "ea506d61-f445-598b-b7b4-71d4e5999d00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" :question/id #uuid "b3abf1cc-eadf-582f-929d-006fffbd1ae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-159965" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Bernoulli random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=6\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ),\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(6\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{2}{1-\\theta }\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{2}{\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{\\theta }+\\frac{2}{\\theta -1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{6(\\theta -1)+2\\theta }{\\theta (\\theta -1)} & =0 \\\\ 6(\\theta -1)+2\\theta  & =0 \\\\ 8\\theta -6 & =0 \\\\ 8\\theta  & =6 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{3}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbe870a-0100-5aae-b454-49e3eb8844b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd968792-04b8-50fc-800f-35d02d77d269" "answer-c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf" "answer-9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6" "answer-0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16" "answer-92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd968792-04b8-50fc-800f-35d02d77d269" :answer/id #uuid "fd968792-04b8-50fc-800f-35d02d77d269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf" :answer/id #uuid "c44e79cb-7368-5b47-96a3-d466cfa63dcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6" :answer/id #uuid "9b090b25-4146-55a8-a5b6-04376c6065c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16" :answer/id #uuid "0450f0af-5d9b-567c-a1ad-d112306dcc16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071" :answer/id #uuid "92c2529a-c481-5299-855e-40b34693e071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad" :question/id #uuid "a6d182d3-6707-59a8-922c-7df2bb097cad" :question/math-academy-id "q-159971" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Poisson random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-5\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-5\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =-5+\\frac{4}{\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5+\\frac{4}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-5\\theta +4}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ -5\\theta +4 & =0 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=\\frac{4}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fb3d4ca8-f088-5bd5-860c-f0291af054cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fb3d4ca8-f088-5bd5-860c-f0291af054cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb3d4ca8-f088-5bd5-860c-f0291af054cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" "answer-7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" "answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" "answer-dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" "answer-7bb1b0f3-0b13-5864-83a1-105f6280eef0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" :answer/id #uuid "7399eea1-69ca-595e-a652-c19bcbe640a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" :answer/id #uuid "7f993abd-7f38-5e5f-8e1e-36f70f05aa31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer/id #uuid "44a118ec-41f7-5413-a4c8-32753ff0ebca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" :answer/id #uuid "dff4b107-b57d-540e-93c5-bfef91bdbf80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7bb1b0f3-0b13-5864-83a1-105f6280eef0" :answer/id #uuid "7bb1b0f3-0b13-5864-83a1-105f6280eef0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-953449db-a540-520d-adff-108b01b9d257" :question/id #uuid "953449db-a540-520d-adff-108b01b9d257" :question/math-academy-id "q-159970" :question/problem "Given that the log-likelihood function for a particular sample of independent Poisson random variables is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=-4\\theta +8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡24\n$$\n\nwhat is the maximum likelihood estimate $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}$ from this sample?" :question/worked-solution "In order to find the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta ,$ we calculate the derivative of the log-likelihood function, set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $\\theta .$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative of $l(\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}l}{\\text{d}\\theta } & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-4\\theta +8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡24) \\\\  & =-4+\\frac{8}{\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we set the derivative equal to $0$ and solve for $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+\\frac{8}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-4\\theta +8}{\\theta } & =0 \\\\ -4\\theta +8 & =0 \\\\ \\theta  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for this sample, the maximum likelihood estimate of $\\theta $ is $\\overset{^}{\\,\\theta \\,}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/id #uuid "332d2628-c9ca-5acc-836b-f4adcf66f467" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f44da59-7cd2-5b7d-af6d-baec2d76fd01" "answer-05ec69c2-402d-585f-8677-fa0507e34591" "answer-fe90cb0a-c53d-50aa-be27-b8f0505c19f5" "answer-f9cad