 :question/math-academy-id "q-148310" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=4,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=1,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=1.2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=4+1-2\\cdot 1.2=2.6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98eba2e3-746d-555e-a1fb-96940568baf2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98eba2e3-746d-555e-a1fb-96940568baf2" :answer-field/id #uuid "98eba2e3-746d-555e-a1fb-96940568baf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d440fa76-ed34-5fa7-ba1a-4299f3912c16" "answer-a81e4ece-d7f2-5c11-822e-db92a71d403c" "answer-cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" "answer-eeac769e-1c7d-5f17-9702-eee8738c6039" "answer-c23cc5cc-232d-50cb-bf03-dcc14216ffbb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d440fa76-ed34-5fa7-ba1a-4299f3912c16" :answer/id #uuid "d440fa76-ed34-5fa7-ba1a-4299f3912c16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a81e4ece-d7f2-5c11-822e-db92a71d403c" :answer/id #uuid "a81e4ece-d7f2-5c11-822e-db92a71d403c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" :answer/id #uuid "cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eeac769e-1c7d-5f17-9702-eee8738c6039" :answer/id #uuid "eeac769e-1c7d-5f17-9702-eee8738c6039" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c23cc5cc-232d-50cb-bf03-dcc14216ffbb" :answer/id #uuid "c23cc5cc-232d-50cb-bf03-dcc14216ffbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bade78ae-2b02-5df2-9480-36d57f4806a3" :question/id #uuid "bade78ae-2b02-5df2-9480-36d57f4806a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-148307" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{8},$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{3}{4},$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\frac{5}{16}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{3}{4}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{16}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d797f9f7-f609-5c5e-ba78-717e24c03bac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d797f9f7-f609-5c5e-ba78-717e24c03bac" :answer-field/id #uuid "d797f9f7-f609-5c5e-ba78-717e24c03bac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a-0647d6a9d350" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b5b6e8f-5bc3-560d-8885-95ce43bf6cca" "answer-e8d75129-0300-58cb-992b-b2f66d1dd767" "answer-b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a-0647d6a9d350" "answer-d00ac744-2b33-547b-8327-668720b71a82" "answer-f787f52b-7c28-5038-948b-07653cdbb173"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b5b6e8f-5bc3-560d-8885-95ce43bf6cca" :answer/id #uuid "6b5b6e8f-5bc3-560d-8885-95ce43bf6cca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8d75129-0300-58cb-992b-b2f66d1dd767" :answer/id #uuid "e8d75129-0300-58cb-992b-b2f66d1dd767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a-0647d6a9d350" :answer/id #uuid "b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a-0647d6a9d350" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d00ac744-2b33-547b-8327-668720b71a82" :answer/id #uuid "d00ac744-2b33-547b-8327-668720b71a82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f787f52b-7c28-5038-948b-07653cdbb173" :answer/id #uuid "f787f52b-7c28-5038-948b-07653cdbb173" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-079f02ad-9ee0-58ac-bead-d4394104b125" :question/id #uuid "079f02ad-9ee0-58ac-bead-d4394104b125" :question/math-academy-id "q-148325" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=2,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=4,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=3.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X+2Y] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 2+{2}^{2}\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =2+16+12 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6e9903df-3d0e-558c-a936-1e634a7a414f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6e9903df-3d0e-558c-a936-1e634a7a414f" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9903df-3d0e-558c-a936-1e634a7a414f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9f45a7c-cd89-5de7-919f-40df36a8e57e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4b45f6f-0aca-5265-a86f-dc576861c0d9" "answer-11b0f9e8-5bed-5e28-8aa4-8891548dbee5" "answer-e9f45a7c-cd89-5de7-919f-40df36a8e57e" "answer-fb52047a-64f1-55c6-bcdc-b7d871b74bba" "answer-25c6b3fe-797b-5c3b-b5d3-ad2fbd9060da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4b45f6f-0aca-5265-a86f-dc576861c0d9" :answer/id #uuid "c4b45f6f-0aca-5265-a86f-dc576861c0d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11b0f9e8-5bed-5e28-8aa4-8891548dbee5" :answer/id #uuid "11b0f9e8-5bed-5e28-8aa4-8891548dbee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9f45a7c-cd89-5de7-919f-40df36a8e57e" :answer/id #uuid "e9f45a7c-cd89-5de7-919f-40df36a8e57e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb52047a-64f1-55c6-bcdc-b7d871b74bba" :answer/id #uuid "fb52047a-64f1-55c6-bcdc-b7d871b74bba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25c6b3fe-797b-5c3b-b5d3-ad2fbd9060da" :answer/id #uuid "25c6b3fe-797b-5c3b-b5d3-ad2fbd9060da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d139a777-1244-5988-9682-4e7da954d933" :question/id #uuid "d139a777-1244-5988-9682-4e7da954d933" :question/math-academy-id "q-148329" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=3,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=5,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=1.$ Find $\\text{Var}[3X-4Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X-4Y] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-4)^{2}\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =27+80-24 \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-44a50128-f069-562c-b225-44f83d8c3770"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44a50128-f069-562c-b225-44f83d8c3770" :answer-field/id #uuid "44a50128-f069-562c-b225-44f83d8c3770" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-042d7ca6-0980-5b74-8fb1-e853458aefff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1fe11208-1cf5-5ebb-b9ae-1cfd9d864264" "answer-5212a1f4-14ce-5363-9b60-7fca91d0f9cc" "answer-3ed17f21-46a7-5c9d-badf-51e6f9909dd1" "answer-5b321d10-02bd-5f8b-9dc8-387f61a077be" "answer-042d7ca6-0980-5b74-8fb1-e853458aefff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fe11208-1cf5-5ebb-b9ae-1cfd9d864264" :answer/id #uuid "1fe11208-1cf5-5ebb-b9ae-1cfd9d864264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5212a1f4-14ce-5363-9b60-7fca91d0f9cc" :answer/id #uuid "5212a1f4-14ce-5363-9b60-7fca91d0f9cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "66" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ed17f21-46a7-5c9d-badf-51e6f9909dd1" :answer/id #uuid "3ed17f21-46a7-5c9d-badf-51e6f9909dd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b321d10-02bd-5f8b-9dc8-387f61a077be" :answer/id #uuid "5b321d10-02bd-5f8b-9dc8-387f61a077be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-042d7ca6-0980-5b74-8fb1-e853458aefff" :answer/id #uuid "042d7ca6-0980-5b74-8fb1-e853458aefff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "83" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188783 :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=5,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=11,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=4.$ Find $\\text{Var}[2X-3Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-3Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 5+(-3)^{2}\\cdot 11+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20+99-48 \\\\  & =71.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186186978 :answer-field/correct 17592186186979 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" :question/id #uuid "af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-148331" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.1,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.7,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[7X-4Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X-4Y] & ={7}^{2}\\cdot 0.1+(-4)^{2}\\cdot 0.7+2\\cdot 7\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =4.9+11.2-11.2 \\\\  & =4.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6e79e9c9-3fca-53e4-af45-03318ed7bb0c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6e79e9c9-3fca-53e4-af45-03318ed7bb0c" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e79e9c9-3fca-53e4-af45-03318ed7bb0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4a635d19-edad-56dc-9f3e-8fb6e159993d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a9e6b505-6b6f-5ef8-ab62-f5ba3765a1d6" "answer-5ec9220d-acc9-5f8a-b548-2aa15bc850f8" "answer-13b69179-3383-516b-9efb-08040395b10b" "answer-4a635d19-edad-56dc-9f3e-8fb6e159993d" "answer-2feeb232-e56f-552c-962e-5f79343f3fba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9e6b505-6b6f-5ef8-ab62-f5ba3765a1d6" :answer/id #uuid "a9e6b505-6b6f-5ef8-ab62-f5ba3765a1d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ec9220d-acc9-5f8a-b548-2aa15bc850f8" :answer/id #uuid "5ec9220d-acc9-5f8a-b548-2aa15bc850f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13b69179-3383-516b-9efb-08040395b10b" :answer/id #uuid "13b69179-3383-516b-9efb-08040395b10b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a635d19-edad-56dc-9f3e-8fb6e159993d" :answer/id #uuid "4a635d19-edad-56dc-9f3e-8fb6e159993d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2feeb232-e56f-552c-962e-5f79343f3fba" :answer/id #uuid "2feeb232-e56f-552c-962e-5f79343f3fba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1e6dcf9d-d6cd-51ac-b73d-58cf9701a199" :question/id #uuid "1e6dcf9d-d6cd-51ac-b73d-58cf9701a199" :question/math-academy-id "q-148330" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.24,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.06,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.08.$ Find $\\text{Var}[2X-8Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-8Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 0.24+(-8)^{2}\\cdot 0.06+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-8)\\cdot 0.08 \\\\  & =0.96+3.84-2.56 \\\\  & =2.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b2574087-a149-5760-a3e0-95a498fe4957"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b2574087-a149-5760-a3e0-95a498fe4957" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2574087-a149-5760-a3e0-95a498fe4957" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a7330edf-fd61-584c-a0ef-021af49ab7e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-909907e4-2fff-5429-908d-172891d594e7" "answer-3cdc858f-23d2-52f7-803a-0d8ca2c80206" "answer-60036dd0-65af-52cb-a069-bd37caf7adfd" "answer-a7330edf-fd61-584c-a0ef-021af49ab7e0" "answer-1730b466-edec-5557-8be0-4765900d97d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-909907e4-2fff-5429-908d-172891d594e7" :answer/id #uuid "909907e4-2fff-5429-908d-172891d594e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cdc858f-23d2-52f7-803a-0d8ca2c80206" :answer/id #uuid "3cdc858f-23d2-52f7-803a-0d8ca2c80206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.51" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60036dd0-65af-52cb-a069-bd37caf7adfd" :answer/id #uuid "60036dd0-65af-52cb-a069-bd37caf7adfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.78" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7330edf-fd61-584c-a0ef-021af49ab7e0" :answer/id #uuid "a7330edf-fd61-584c-a0ef-021af49ab7e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1730b466-edec-5557-8be0-4765900d97d7" :answer/id #uuid "1730b466-edec-5557-8be0-4765900d97d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.53" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188787 :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[2X+3Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ | $0.8$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.2+1\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =0.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.2+{1}^{2}\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.8-{0.8}^{2} \\\\  & =0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =1.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 0.4+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2.8-{1.6}^{2} \\\\  & =0.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We compute $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+1\\cdot 1\\cdot f(1,1)+1\\cdot 2\\cdot f(1,2) \\\\  & =0+0+1\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.3-0.8\\cdot 1.6 \\\\  & =0.02.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X+3Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 0.16+{3}^{2}\\cdot 0.24+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot 0.02 \\\\  & =0.64+2.16+0.24 \\\\  & =3.04.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186187002 :answer-field/correct 17592186187004 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-43034259-a22b-5dd7-b48f-a2ed42e0b13d" :question/id #uuid "43034259-a22b-5dd7-b48f-a2ed42e0b13d" :question/math-academy-id "q-148346" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.7 \\\\  & =1.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.3+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.7 \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =2.8-{1.4}^{2} \\\\  & =0.84.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.5+1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{1}^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =0.5-{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We find $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot f(0,0)+0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+2\\cdot 0\\cdot f(2,0)+2\\cdot 1\\cdot f(2,1) \\\\  & =0+0+0+2\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =0.6-1.4\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X-Y] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 0.84+(-1)^{2}\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-0.1) \\\\  & =7.56+0.25+0.6 \\\\  & =8.41.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-338abd00-bef7-5a0e-90d2-b18f076c9de2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-338abd00-bef7-5a0e-90d2-b18f076c9de2" :answer-field/id #uuid "338abd00-bef7-5a0e-90d2-b18f076c9de2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8b1cefcd-2445-53e0-9e6c-8133a9228e46" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49ada7d0-4cef-56d8-bcef-b0502f40aca2" "answer-468fa4dd-aa55-5c1c-adbf-af8f95c32adb" "answer-720fce8b-4a4c-5001-875c-151d8e621507" "answer-8b1cefcd-2445-53e0-9e6c-8133a9228e46" "answer-5470918e-e06a-57bb-b01a-7b0ef04bc1bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49ada7d0-4cef-56d8-bcef-b0502f40aca2" :answer/id #uuid "49ada7d0-4cef-56d8-bcef-b0502f40aca2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.69" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-468fa4dd-aa55-5c1c-adbf-af8f95c32adb" :answer/id #uuid "468fa4dd-aa55-5c1c-adbf-af8f95c32adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-720fce8b-4a4c-5001-875c-151d8e621507" :answer/id #uuid "720fce8b-4a4c-5001-875c-151d8e621507" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b1cefcd-2445-53e0-9e6c-8133a9228e46" :answer/id #uuid "8b1cefcd-2445-53e0-9e6c-8133a9228e46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.41" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5470918e-e06a-57bb-b01a-7b0ef04bc1bb" :answer/id #uuid "5470918e-e06a-57bb-b01a-7b0ef04bc1bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c291da1-e168-5e62-8128-2d4c3d94af53" :question/id #uuid "7c291da1-e168-5e62-8128-2d4c3d94af53" :question/math-academy-id "q-148351" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3X+4Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.55$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.45+4\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =2.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.45+{4}^{2}\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =8.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =8.8-{2.2}^{2} \\\\  & =3.96.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2.5-{1.5}^{2} \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We find $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+4\\cdot 1\\cdot f(4,1)+4\\cdot 2\\cdot f(4,2) \\\\  & =0+0+4\\cdot 0.2+8\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =3.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =3.6-2.2\\cdot 1.5 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X+4Y] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 3.96+{4}^{2}\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =35.64+4+7.2 \\\\  & =46.84.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a4a349e6-751b-52e3-889b-23f3be2178b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a4a349e6-751b-52e3-889b-23f3be2178b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4a349e6-751b-52e3-889b-23f3be2178b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eb7482b1-371a-5ba6-941f-1144ea4bfa78" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b594c8db-9430-5a22-b797-08e58983a322" "answer-c7b3b1e0-de02-59a0-8905-c06056522de3" "answer-bb3807e9-784b-5046-9fb0-1d5c63a1fe7f" "answer-eb7482b1-371a-5ba6-941f-1144ea4bfa78" "answer-2e3129f4-5fbf-5a1b-8819-be0cbbf448d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b594c8db-9430-5a22-b797-08e58983a322" :answer/id #uuid "b594c8db-9430-5a22-b797-08e58983a322" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32.56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7b3b1e0-de02-59a0-8905-c06056522de3" :answer/id #uuid "c7b3b1e0-de02-59a0-8905-c06056522de3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "39.62" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb3807e9-784b-5046-9fb0-1d5c63a1fe7f" :answer/id #uuid "bb3807e9-784b-5046-9fb0-1d5c63a1fe7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "43.86" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb7482b1-371a-5ba6-941f-1144ea4bfa78" :answer/id #uuid "eb7482b1-371a-5ba6-941f-1144ea4bfa78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "46.84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e3129f4-5fbf-5a1b-8819-be0cbbf448d2" :answer/id #uuid "2e3129f4-5fbf-5a1b-8819-be0cbbf448d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188786 :question/problem "Consider two random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=2,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=4,$ mixed moment $\\text{E}[XY]=10,$ and second raw moments $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=9$ and $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=20.$ Find the variance of $2X-5Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =9-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =20-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =10-2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-5Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 5+(-5)^{2}\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =20+100-40 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186186996 :answer-field/correct 17592186186997 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-e96228aa-7e46-5ce5-96d2-d22e87559f00" :question/id #uuid "e96228aa-7e46-5ce5-96d2-d22e87559f00" :question/math-academy-id "q-148348" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3X-2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.55+2\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.55+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =1.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =1.8-{0.9}^{2} \\\\  & =0.99.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2.5-{1.5}^{2} \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We find $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+2\\cdot 1\\cdot f(2,1)+2\\cdot 2\\cdot f(2,2) \\\\  & =0+0+2\\cdot 0.2+4\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.4-0.9\\cdot 1.5 \\\\  & =0.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X-2Y] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 0.99+(-2)^{2}\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0.05 \\\\  & =8.91+1-0.6 \\\\  & =9.31.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e551be10-49d7-5b00-a0da-a0e8ce37b373"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e551be10-49d7-5b00-a0da-a0e8ce37b373" :answer-field/id #uuid "e551be10-49d7-5b00-a0da-a0e8ce37b373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f9906a6-c4a0-571b-a9fe-b0988e41fc63" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7f42f492-9fe9-5724-b584-66ae829fc7d9" "answer-e7dcec73-2add-5548-aec0-fc739525b3dc" "answer-3f9906a6-c4a0-571b-a9fe-b0988e41fc63" "answer-070e6987-47d6-5f73-9aa9-86a2d5cb82ec" "answer-a7d64e3b-21c0-551e-b123-974f1cbd894d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f42f492-9fe9-5724-b584-66ae829fc7d9" :answer/id #uuid "7f42f492-9fe9-5724-b584-66ae829fc7d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7dcec73-2add-5548-aec0-fc739525b3dc" :answer/id #uuid "e7dcec73-2add-5548-aec0-fc739525b3dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10.51" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f9906a6-c4a0-571b-a9fe-b0988e41fc63" :answer/id #uuid "3f9906a6-c4a0-571b-a9fe-b0988e41fc63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.31" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-070e6987-47d6-5f73-9aa9-86a2d5cb82ec" :answer/id #uuid "070e6987-47d6-5f73-9aa9-86a2d5cb82ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7d64e3b-21c0-551e-b123-974f1cbd894d" :answer/id #uuid "a7d64e3b-21c0-551e-b123-974f1cbd894d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.85" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e0b47f27-b72b-520b-9e5b-9f7678a818fc" :question/id #uuid "e0b47f27-b72b-520b-9e5b-9f7678a818fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-148399" :question/problem "For three random variables ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},$ and ${X}_{3},$ we have the following variances and covariances:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]=3,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]=0.5,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}]=1.5\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]=-0.75,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]=-3.5,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]=4\\,\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}+4{X}_{2}+6{X}_{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},…,{X}_{n}$ are random variables, and ${a}_{1},…,{a}_{n}$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{X}_{i}]={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{i}]+2{\\sum }_{i<j}{a}_{i}{a}_{j}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{i},{X}_{j}].\n$$\n\nHence, for $n=3$ random variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{a}_{1}{X}_{1}+{a}_{2}{X}_{2}+{a}_{3}{X}_{3}] & ={a}_{1}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}+4{X}_{2}+6{X}_{3}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 3+{4}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{6}^{2}\\cdot 1.5 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 1\\cdot 4\\cdot (-0.75)+2\\cdot 1\\cdot 6\\cdot (-3.5)+2\\cdot 4\\cdot 6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =3+8+54-6-42+192 \\\\  & =209.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7013aeae-6a4b-54c0-a7ce-c4c928ca841d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7013aeae-6a4b-54c0-a7ce-c4c928ca841d" :answer-field/id #uuid "7013aeae-6a4b-54c0-a7ce-c4c928ca841d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-78534fc9-e405-57b5-9b6d-30c8b94d0b38" :answer-field/choices ["answer-83f959c6-ecaf-52c2-83d2-c523d4096a30" "answer-f22af125-b5c3-5190-b0ab-21b1cca3cf1e" "answer-78534fc9-e405-57b5-9b6d-30c8b94d0b38" "answer-a508ac9a-d3b2-5d7e-9955-803b8f2e995c" "answer-845e1070-adec-50b4-baf7-02a5443b23d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83f959c6-ecaf-52c2-83d2-c523d4096a30" :answer/id #uuid "83f959c6-ecaf-52c2-83d2-c523d4096a30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "185" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f22af125-b5c3-5190-b0ab-21b1cca3cf1e" :answer/id #uuid "f22af125-b5c3-5190-b0ab-21b1cca3cf1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "196" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78534fc9-e405-57b5-9b6d-30c8b94d0b38" :answer/id #uuid "78534fc9-e405-57b5-9b6d-30c8b94d0b38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "209" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a508ac9a-d3b2-5d7e-9955-803b8f2e995c" :answer/id #uuid "a508ac9a-d3b2-5d7e-9955-803b8f2e995c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "217" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-845e1070-adec-50b4-baf7-02a5443b23d9" :answer/id #uuid "845e1070-adec-50b4-baf7-02a5443b23d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "224" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188784 :question/problem "For three random variables ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},$ and ${X}_{3},$ we have the following variances and covariances:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]=5,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]=4,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}]=2\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]=3,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]=1,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]=2\\,\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+4{X}_{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},…,{X}_{n}$ are random variables, and ${a}_{1},…,{a}_{n}$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{X}_{i}]={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{i}]+2{\\sum }_{i<j}{a}_{i}{a}_{j}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{i},{X}_{j}].\n$$\n\nHence, for $n=3$ random variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{a}_{1}{X}_{1}+{a}_{2}{X}_{2}+{a}_{3}{X}_{3}] & ={a}_{1}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+4{X}_{3}] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 4+{4}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =45+16+32+36+24+32 \\\\  & =185.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186186984 :answer-field/correct 17592186186987 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186189413 :tutorial/content "Given two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ the variance of the sum or difference of these variables is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\pm Y] = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y] \\pm 2\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y],\n$$\n\nwhere $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$ We'll prove this formula at the end of the lesson.\n\nNote that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y]= 0,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\pm Y] = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y].\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186189414 :tutorial/content "If $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX + bY] = a^2 \\textrm{Var}[X] + b^2 \\textrm{Var}[Y] + 2ab \\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nIf $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 0,$ and we recover the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX + bY] = a^2 \\textrm{Var}[X] + b^2 \\textrm{Var}[Y] .\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186189421 :tutorial/content "Let's prove the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X+ Y] = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y] + 2\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y]\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of variance and using the linearity of expectation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X+Y] & =\\text{E}[((X+Y)-\\text{E}[X+Y])^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[((X-\\text{E}[X])+(Y-\\text{E}[Y]))^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}+(Y-\\text{E}[Y])^{2}+2(X-\\text{E}[X])(Y-\\text{E}[Y])].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDistributing the expected value, and using the fact that $\\textrm{E}[aX] = a\\cdot \\textrm{E}[X]$ for constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X+Y] & =\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}+(Y-\\text{E}[Y])^{2}+2(X-\\text{E}[X])(Y-\\text{E}[Y])] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}]+\\text{E}[(Y-\\text{E}[Y])^{2}]+2\\cdot \\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])(Y-\\text{E}[Y])] \\\\  & =\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]+2\\text{Cov}[X,Y]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nas required. \n\nThe proof for the difference between two random variables is similar." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188522 :activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186125074 :question/answer-fields 17592186123044] [:db/retract 17592186125078 :question/answer-fields 17592186123068] {:db/id 17592186124463 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4bf356ec-77aa-55f5-9268-fd51c57a8d9c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4bf356ec-77aa-55f5-9268-fd51c57a8d9c" :question/id #uuid "4bf356ec-77aa-55f5-9268-fd51c57a8d9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71400" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)$, find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,1,1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(1,1,1) & =\\frac{1}{1}\\,i+\\frac{1}{1}\\,j+\\frac{1}{1}\\,k \\\\  & =i+j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $i+j+k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f14cf0d4-83ef-5fb3-b242-66382b80f326"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f14cf0d4-83ef-5fb3-b242-66382b80f326" :answer-field/id #uuid "f14cf0d4-83ef-5fb3-b242-66382b80f326" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-47b2da7a-a030-51c5-b002-05391f108200" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c8f30ca4-75c7-5d71-83ef-390f43fece84" "answer-1fc28fd4-0332-5dca-9124-fbc2512f4f90" "answer-47b2da7a-a030-51c5-b002-05391f108200" "answer-e8e5fc00-b4cc-5045-8cb1-ac186e6219f3" "answer-e2579daa-2b83-50d8-a9be-1387a386e9ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8f30ca4-75c7-5d71-83ef-390f43fece84" :answer/id #uuid "c8f30ca4-75c7-5d71-83ef-390f43fece84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}i+j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fc28fd4-0332-5dca-9124-fbc2512f4f90" :answer/id #uuid "1fc28fd4-0332-5dca-9124-fbc2512f4f90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47b2da7a-a030-51c5-b002-05391f108200" :answer/id #uuid "47b2da7a-a030-51c5-b002-05391f108200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8e5fc00-b4cc-5045-8cb1-ac186e6219f3" :answer/id #uuid "e8e5fc00-b4cc-5045-8cb1-ac186e6219f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2579daa-2b83-50d8-a9be-1387a386e9ea" :answer/id #uuid "e2579daa-2b83-50d8-a9be-1387a386e9ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124462 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-28dded9d-d02a-5f94-8a43-d32ef32c8465"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-28dded9d-d02a-5f94-8a43-d32ef32c8465" :question/id #uuid "28dded9d-d02a-5f94-8a43-d32ef32c8465" :question/math-academy-id "q-130720" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve ${x}^{3}{y}^{2}=2x+y.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}{y}^{2} & =2x+y \\\\ {x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2x-y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2x-y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(-1,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(-1,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(-1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2x-y)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2x-y)j \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-2)\\,i+(2{x}^{3}y-1)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,1) & =(3(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}-2)\\,i+(2(-1)^{3}(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =\\,i-3\\,j \\\\  & =⟨1,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(-1,1)=⟨1,-3⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(1,-3).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-(-1)}{1} & =\\frac{y-1}{(-3)} \\\\ -3(x+1) & =y-1 \\\\ -3x-3 & =y-1 \\\\ 3x+y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdf514b2-8d3a-5a58-a6b9-5e62c2d37fa5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdf514b2-8d3a-5a58-a6b9-5e62c2d37fa5" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf514b2-8d3a-5a58-a6b9-5e62c2d37fa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-253ca439-cd38-5c0a-a233-00c9ea58b381" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdd0a5cd-65c6-58a5-ac60-ab333212dddc" "answer-253ca439-cd38-5c0a-a233-00c9ea58b381" "answer-6545d507-c4ab-5302-a22d-62c4ef0a3e20" "answer-1a0e0626-6248-5b0f-8302-6f527732a13c" "answer-48db2746-13e6-5da9-a526-f85be7161a7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdd0a5cd-65c6-58a5-ac60-ab333212dddc" :answer/id #uuid "fdd0a5cd-65c6-58a5-ac60-ab333212dddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+y+1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-253ca439-cd38-5c0a-a233-00c9ea58b381" :answer/id #uuid "253ca439-cd38-5c0a-a233-00c9ea58b381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+y+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6545d507-c4ab-5302-a22d-62c4ef0a3e20" :answer/id #uuid "6545d507-c4ab-5302-a22d-62c4ef0a3e20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a0e0626-6248-5b0f-8302-6f527732a13c" :answer/id #uuid "1a0e0626-6248-5b0f-8302-6f527732a13c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y+3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48db2746-13e6-5da9-a526-f85be7161a7c" :answer/id #uuid "48db2746-13e6-5da9-a526-f85be7161a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-0ef48a11-b676-522a-82bb-9f39665ac76e" :activity/id #uuid "0ef48a11-b676-522a-82bb-9f39665ac76e" :activity/title "The Gradient as a Normal Vector" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050027 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-2598a4b3-3e2b-55cf-8762-35fa24bff20e" "step-628d3218-9eb5-5ad9-a24c-b47a38223247" "step-7d9f5645-ab76-539c-abb6-92fcd4f5fb7f" "step-17075a61-c9d0-5adb-a8b2-23c29d75a027" "step-6839775f-3cbd-5361-8538-0f08a1251e91"] :activity/first-step "step-2598a4b3-3e2b-55cf-8762-35fa24bff20e" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2598a4b3-3e2b-55cf-8762-35fa24bff20e" :step/id #uuid "2598a4b3-3e2b-55cf-8762-35fa24bff20e" :step/content 17592186125074 :step/next "step-628d3218-9eb5-5ad9-a24c-b47a38223247" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-628d3218-9eb5-5ad9-a24c-b47a38223247" :step/id #uuid "628d3218-9eb5-5ad9-a24c-b47a38223247" :step/content 17592186125078 :step/next "step-7d9f5645-ab76-539c-abb6-92fcd4f5fb7f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7d9f5645-ab76-539c-abb6-92fcd4f5fb7f" :step/id #uuid "7d9f5645-ab76-539c-abb6-92fcd4f5fb7f" :step/content "question-4bf356ec-77aa-55f5-9268-fd51c57a8d9c" :step/next "step-17075a61-c9d0-5adb-a8b2-23c29d75a027" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-17075a61-c9d0-5adb-a8b2-23c29d75a027" :step/id #uuid "17075a61-c9d0-5adb-a8b2-23c29d75a027" :step/content 17592186403468 :step/next "step-6839775f-3cbd-5361-8538-0f08a1251e91" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6839775f-3cbd-5361-8538-0f08a1251e91" :step/id #uuid "6839775f-3cbd-5361-8538-0f08a1251e91" :step/content "question-28dded9d-d02a-5f94-8a43-d32ef32c8465" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198370 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-216ab53f-9c7f-5387-ad09-67452d907209"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-216ab53f-9c7f-5387-ad09-67452d907209" :question/id #uuid "216ab53f-9c7f-5387-ad09-67452d907209" :question/math-academy-id "q-160572" :question/problem "Consider all non-critical points of the transformation $T:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y)\\to (u(x,y),v(x,y))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}xy \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $u(x,y)=xy$ and $v(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}.$ \n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =y & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =x \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =\\frac{2x}{y} & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ \\frac{2x}{y} & -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =y\\cdot (-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})-x\\cdot \\frac{2x}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\  & =-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3v}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3aa3cd04-7b64-5645-9bfe-bb149f8d1b73"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3aa3cd04-7b64-5645-9bfe-bb149f8d1b73" :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa3cd04-7b64-5645-9bfe-bb149f8d1b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c4ff2ce6-b380-5ab9-9fa2-41399e5c2bf3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4ff2ce6-b380-5ab9-9fa2-41399e5c2bf3" "answer-a0e1f31b-7a73-5f60-aa37-ebb1960532b8" "answer-1da512ca-3f7f-55fa-ba92-0e0c6f6c21be" "answer-cabf98b2-4e8b-519a-86a9-7f344c20fcb7" "answer-3f9f7694-d0a1-5a9c-8f7b-8ada526129f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4ff2ce6-b380-5ab9-9fa2-41399e5c2bf3" :answer/id #uuid "c4ff2ce6-b380-5ab9-9fa2-41399e5c2bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0e1f31b-7a73-5f60-aa37-ebb1960532b8" :answer/id #uuid "a0e1f31b-7a73-5f60-aa37-ebb1960532b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{v}{u}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1da512ca-3f7f-55fa-ba92-0e0c6f6c21be" :answer/id #uuid "1da512ca-3f7f-55fa-ba92-0e0c6f6c21be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cabf98b2-4e8b-519a-86a9-7f344c20fcb7" :answer/id #uuid "cabf98b2-4e8b-519a-86a9-7f344c20fcb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f9f7694-d0a1-5a9c-8f7b-8ada526129f3" :answer/id #uuid "3f9f7694-d0a1-5a9c-8f7b-8ada526129f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{u}{3v}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d4d7c1e7-1e75-5e96-a1f2-125d61b017ca" :activity/id #uuid "d4d7c1e7-1e75-5e96-a1f2-125d61b017ca" :activity/title "The Inverse Function Theorem" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048251 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-e82f2471-fe74-5e55-b55f-d5691e572e48" "step-631c1ffc-cc2d-54ee-9534-d0fd945d1a0f" "step-51036647-b610-5b0a-9fd7-d9d58d8980da" "step-139d7e34-eb4e-5c83-930d-e178bce0f1f7" "step-96a24d2f-6bfd-5bae-b385-4ad5b9f4b243"] :activity/first-step "step-e82f2471-fe74-5e55-b55f-d5691e572e48" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-e82f2471-fe74-5e55-b55f-d5691e572e48" :step/id #uuid "e82f2471-fe74-5e55-b55f-d5691e572e48" :step/content 17592186351282 :step/next "step-631c1ffc-cc2d-54ee-9534-d0fd945d1a0f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-631c1ffc-cc2d-54ee-9534-d0fd945d1a0f" :step/id #uuid "631c1ffc-cc2d-54ee-9534-d0fd945d1a0f" :step/content 17592186404163 :step/next "step-51036647-b610-5b0a-9fd7-d9d58d8980da" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-51036647-b610-5b0a-9fd7-d9d58d8980da" :step/id #uuid "51036647-b610-5b0a-9fd7-d9d58d8980da" :step/content "question-216ab53f-9c7f-5387-ad09-67452d907209" :step/next "step-139d7e34-eb4e-5c83-930d-e178bce0f1f7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-139d7e34-eb4e-5c83-930d-e178bce0f1f7" :step/id #uuid "139d7e34-eb4e-5c83-930d-e178bce0f1f7" :step/content 17592186278314 :step/next "step-96a24d2f-6bfd-5bae-b385-4ad5b9f4b243" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-96a24d2f-6bfd-5bae-b385-4ad5b9f4b243" :step/id #uuid "96a24d2f-6bfd-5bae-b385-4ad5b9f4b243" :step/content 17592186278316 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133736 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-01e96138-a1bd-5aa7-aa98-7c5862390efd" "question-3cfc1cc8-75ac-58cb-baba-115d9b2db8af"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-01e96138-a1bd-5aa7-aa98-7c5862390efd" :question/id #uuid "01e96138-a1bd-5aa7-aa98-7c5862390efd" :question/math-academy-id "q-185123" :question/problem "$(-70)^{2}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To work out $(-70)^{2},$ we multiply $-70$ by itself:\n\n$$\n(-70)^{2}=(-70)\\cdot (-70)=4,900\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-46e559e6-e4ac-5019-a50d-551c23e251b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-46e559e6-e4ac-5019-a50d-551c23e251b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "46e559e6-e4ac-5019-a50d-551c23e251b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-971a476b-092c-5d91-b8fa-81b2b6ab3d00" :answer-field/choices ["answer-971a476b-092c-5d91-b8fa-81b2b6ab3d00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-971a476b-092c-5d91-b8fa-81b2b6ab3d00" :answer/id #uuid "971a476b-092c-5d91-b8fa-81b2b6ab3d00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4900" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078611 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-454efe3b-e281-5051-bb7a-cf90c5710624"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-454efe3b-e281-5051-bb7a-cf90c5710624" :question/id #uuid "454efe3b-e281-5051-bb7a-cf90c5710624" :question/math-academy-id "q-75596" :question/problem "What is the constant term in the expression $\\frac{2}{3}+6a-4b?$" :question/worked-solution "The expression has three terms: $\\frac{2}{3}$, $6a$, and $-4b.$  The only term that does not contain any variables is $\\frac{2}{3}$, so $\\frac{2}{3}$ is the constant term." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4199400-b56c-59e9-9b3d-11651577e755"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4199400-b56c-59e9-9b3d-11651577e755" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4199400-b56c-59e9-9b3d-11651577e755" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7fa11361-56d4-5ceb-927c-caac0ea52b15" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59d32871-b127-5f6c-abbd-d1dfc584422f" "answer-3fd8663f-2fcb-5208-a496-a309cc26dd51" "answer-7e5b6940-eace-5aff-ac22-af6a6f97e50c" "answer-df0a8216-29ab-5dcc-bed2-d4bf11ad9854" "answer-7fa11361-56d4-5ceb-927c-caac0ea52b15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59d32871-b127-5f6c-abbd-d1dfc584422f" :answer/id #uuid "59d32871-b127-5f6c-abbd-d1dfc584422f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fd8663f-2fcb-5208-a496-a309cc26dd51" :answer/id #uuid "3fd8663f-2fcb-5208-a496-a309cc26dd51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e5b6940-eace-5aff-ac22-af6a6f97e50c" :answer/id #uuid "7e5b6940-eace-5aff-ac22-af6a6f97e50c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df0a8216-29ab-5dcc-bed2-d4bf11ad9854" :answer/id #uuid "df0a8216-29ab-5dcc-bed2-d4bf11ad9854" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fa11361-56d4-5ceb-927c-caac0ea52b15" :answer/id #uuid "7fa11361-56d4-5ceb-927c-caac0ea52b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179814 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e12935f7-7208-5953-a547-9693833e1308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e12935f7-7208-5953-a547-9693833e1308" :question/id #uuid "e12935f7-7208-5953-a547-9693833e1308" :question/math-academy-id "q-186120" :question/problem "$1.2-5=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $5$ is larger than $1.2,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to carry out the subtraction in the reverse order:\n\n$$\n5-1.2=3.8\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n1.2-5=-3.8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f248478f-3341-58c6-9f8c-098a17912162"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f248478f-3341-58c6-9f8c-098a17912162" :answer-field/id #uuid "f248478f-3341-58c6-9f8c-098a17912162" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-dca033f0-f14b-5230-bf01-67d043b720cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dca033f0-f14b-5230-bf01-67d043b720cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dca033f0-f14b-5230-bf01-67d043b720cc" :answer/id #uuid "dca033f0-f14b-5230-bf01-67d043b720cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-34603e37-b60f-5eb1-996c-5382f05619c6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-34603e37-b60f-5eb1-996c-5382f05619c6" :question/id #uuid "34603e37-b60f-5eb1-996c-5382f05619c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-155548" :question/problem "![](images/86/867e0d53894e1cacac86120e5c79b32071e2b0a4863b445e6d3492392a59461d.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $M,Q,J$\n\nII. $P,O,L$\n\nIII. $L,O,M$" :question/worked-solution "- $M,Q,J$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/7f/7f707d8fbeb9853ccb9441bbdab3b0674c5f51da7f73da73d73ee6592dca04ea.png)\n\n- $P,O,L$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/02/028ae56c8a85699d4d6719df2f80a989f1271e392546d005093319af2365675d.png)\n\n \n\n- $L,O,M$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/bf/bf0579ecbc33ebe2d97dc1b305de0a89b0c22dadd6a11d0e88ac4a36acbd447f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-120ed5ca-accb-5a8e-8311-e6ba2c45c2e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-120ed5ca-accb-5a8e-8311-e6ba2c45c2e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "120ed5ca-accb-5a8e-8311-e6ba2c45c2e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-46afe266-6d3a-5859-a3fe-9e6843b9f2d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09c7191f-9231-5628-b2be-151f0fe75054" "answer-af88dc91-36a7-5516-bde0-5fb4f3671912" "answer-5207156e-3306-5267-bf27-448383fe284d" "answer-85523798-fbc8-51c4-81ec-a6fd45f4f5f6" "answer-46afe266-6d3a-5859-a3fe-9e6843b9f2d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09c7191f-9231-5628-b2be-151f0fe75054" :answer/id #uuid "09c7191f-9231-5628-b2be-151f0fe75054" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af88dc91-36a7-5516-bde0-5fb4f3671912" :answer/id #uuid "af88dc91-36a7-5516-bde0-5fb4f3671912" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5207156e-3306-5267-bf27-448383fe284d" :answer/id #uuid "5207156e-3306-5267-bf27-448383fe284d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85523798-fbc8-51c4-81ec-a6fd45f4f5f6" :answer/id #uuid "85523798-fbc8-51c4-81ec-a6fd45f4f5f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46afe266-6d3a-5859-a3fe-9e6843b9f2d9" :answer/id #uuid "46afe266-6d3a-5859-a3fe-9e6843b9f2d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073899 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-23bd23d2-9b32-5ac7-a70a-faac16c61773" "question-0a27d18e-df05-520d-948c-41b1732464a2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-23bd23d2-9b32-5ac7-a70a-faac16c61773" :question/id #uuid "23bd23d2-9b32-5ac7-a70a-faac16c61773" :question/math-academy-id "q-160597" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(0,2)$  and $(0,5)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/f3/f329376e27ec08d2695db0e6d007e7a7b5342e7737c5d3f45eb524a2b1c2e572.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $3$ units, so the distance equals $3.$\n\n![](images/66/66543bc73667ed70a965db4af2e657ad991660fc1b3a73a6e585943deffd3bbb.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/5d/5ded01b570e62d1e206aa8abd1012121367e60e749d441eb4e6ec7e3b12f6e8a.png)\n\nThe point $(0,5)$ is at a distance of $5$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(0,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $5-2=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6a86050d-8890-58f8-9edb-a6ea2587521d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a86050d-8890-58f8-9edb-a6ea2587521d" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a86050d-8890-58f8-9edb-a6ea2587521d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f773a58-226e-501c-8fe2-a236b4c4f65a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78fb9bb8-f5cd-579b-8da8-ad29d8ac8d2f" "answer-8f773a58-226e-501c-8fe2-a236b4c4f65a" "answer-b0dc1b05-f0bd-55da-a84f-44cdc160d318" "answer-79cf0447-e1e6-5819-a545-67c520d7fb14" "answer-22e3e76f-dc9c-57b8-8257-1bd0e126870c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78fb9bb8-f5cd-579b-8da8-ad29d8ac8d2f" :answer/id #uuid "78fb9bb8-f5cd-579b-8da8-ad29d8ac8d2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f773a58-226e-501c-8fe2-a236b4c4f65a" :answer/id #uuid "8f773a58-226e-501c-8fe2-a236b4c4f65a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0dc1b05-f0bd-55da-a84f-44cdc160d318" :answer/id #uuid "b0dc1b05-f0bd-55da-a84f-44cdc160d318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79cf0447-e1e6-5819-a545-67c520d7fb14" :answer/id #uuid "79cf0447-e1e6-5819-a545-67c520d7fb14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22e3e76f-dc9c-57b8-8257-1bd0e126870c" :answer/id #uuid "22e3e76f-dc9c-57b8-8257-1bd0e126870c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105756 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8670832a-c9ac-5ad5-acea-ff50047338a5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8670832a-c9ac-5ad5-acea-ff50047338a5" :question/id #uuid "8670832a-c9ac-5ad5-acea-ff50047338a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-117935" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3e1675e22ef33aa40b96349c910f04178dd4b11b1e7e97f15a5314977eea914f.png)\n\nWhich vertices are adjacent to $F?$" :question/worked-solution "$F$ is the endpoint of the sides $\\overset{―}{FG}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}.$ Therefore, the vertices $E$ and $G$ are adjacent to $F.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7344e6a-19ec-5e61-9602-eaee720b79b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e51fe53a-9370-5baf-91e6-98eb06fd11fa" "answer-02e1c9af-d060-5bfc-b1e9-24bfc3c85aec" "answer-4843a18c-f231-51a7-86f1-a3a822413c27" "answer-6246fcce-dc76-5572-8d13-e91c256ef040" "answer-dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e51fe53a-9370-5baf-91e6-98eb06fd11fa" :answer/id #uuid "e51fe53a-9370-5baf-91e6-98eb06fd11fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $D$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02e1c9af-d060-5bfc-b1e9-24bfc3c85aec" :answer/id #uuid "02e1c9af-d060-5bfc-b1e9-24bfc3c85aec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $G$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4843a18c-f231-51a7-86f1-a3a822413c27" :answer/id #uuid "4843a18c-f231-51a7-86f1-a3a822413c27" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $E$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6246fcce-dc76-5572-8d13-e91c256ef040" :answer/id #uuid "6246fcce-dc76-5572-8d13-e91c256ef040" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ and $G$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a" :answer/id #uuid "dd251353-2c7e-5ab4-9771-6cd4f927f27a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$E$ and $G$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064358 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/id #uuid "61f14a3a-d997-54ee-80e7-e8241a88c524" :question/math-academy-id "q-181162" :question/problem "The value of $12÷(-5),$ expressed as an **improper fraction** in lowest terms, is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a positive number $(12)$ by a negative one $(-5).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n12÷(-5)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $5$ without any signs: $12÷5=\\frac{12}{5}.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n12÷(-5)=-\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6e0284-0b7f-5c7c-9d1a-d5093d110973" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer/id #uuid "3086bc9e-0fdf-59d0-b482-9782173550b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147595 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/id #uuid "21a2d2fe-461f-5c6a-9efc-076472c2d6af" :question/math-academy-id "q-169408" :question/problem "Anna makes two cakes. The first cake weighs $1,200\\,\\text{g},$ while the second cake weighs $140%$ of the weight of the first. What is the weight of the second cake?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the weight of the first cake, which is $1,200\\,\\text{g}.$ The percentage is $140%,$ and the part is the weight of the second cake.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140%=140÷100=1.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140%=\\frac{140}{100}=\\frac{140÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\times 1,200 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{1,200}{5} \\\\  & =7\\times 240 \\\\  & =1,680\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140%$ of $1,200$ is $1,680.$ So, the weight of the second cake is $1,680\\,\\text{g}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6a6020-2874-502a-b31a-02a3e3de1818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" "answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" "answer-f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" "answer-c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" "answer-f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" :answer/id #uuid "3d493e3b-385a-5107-9343-c1afd5716efe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,500\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer/id #uuid "68969a12-ab8d-5fe8-a14a-06fb1ccbf98d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,680\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" :answer/id #uuid "f5caf7c2-b7e5-5bcd-82ab-296088282d8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,720\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" :answer/id #uuid "c5535379-efbb-5009-b0bb-c57b33664b00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,800\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206" :answer/id #uuid "f32e068b-f6a5-59ea-bb32-923d006f5206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,940\\,\\text{g}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054779 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/id #uuid "9d8b1706-5dbe-56db-8638-95f308211cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-171509" :question/problem "$8(2u-5v)=${{field-1}}\n$u\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$v$" :question/worked-solution "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8(2u-5v) & = \\\\ 8\\cdot 2u+8\\cdot (-5v) & = \\\\ (16u)+(-40v) & = \\\\ 16u-40v\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" "answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "074cf9a5-849c-5c4d-8d92-a3bbdf321b5e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer/id #uuid "1ee77bd5-df0e-510f-b7f2-51e63de54bcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "386eb6df-75b9-5eab-b726-efd4b1504a1b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer/id #uuid "e65f4f12-b4e4-5cf1-a812-0955161571c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/id #uuid "72a5b03b-3213-5354-ab4d-cb82e383745f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119548" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{3}-1\\,\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{(1\\times 3)+1}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{2-4}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-4$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/fd/fd7fc3fedd2dbf8c90592bbedfdc15181eae63e4d2cbd71a4c036b2d75e8921c.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-4}{3}=\\frac{-2}{3}=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/id #uuid "43e0bccd-6b23-5084-88cd-20af6e72cdf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" "answer-233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" "answer-975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" "answer-b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" "answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" :answer/id #uuid "6ee49291-e290-50b6-83d8-095e7de4ef05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" :answer/id #uuid "233ea723-90ba-5735-940f-5b13fb2a72aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" :answer/id #uuid "975bb6ad-0f2c-5252-bd1b-a38be3669eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" :answer/id #uuid "b3fd647d-63c1-548a-8bd3-47160dff89c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer/id #uuid "6b69c0f3-19cd-5195-893f-15c580e17e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074391 :question/problem "There are $18$ parrots and $15$ ducks in a zoo. What number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of parrots to ducks is $6:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $6$ parrots for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ ducks." :question/worked-solution "Since there are $18$ parrots and $15$ ducks, the ratio of parrots to ducks is $18:15.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,18 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,15 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,6 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $6:5$ is equivalent to $18:15.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of parrots to ducks is $6:5\\,$ because there are $6$ parrots for every $5\\,$ ducks.\"\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186072584 :answer-field/correct 17592186072586 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152870 :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are integers?\n\nI. $1$\n\nII. $-2$\n\nIII. $-\\frac{1}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The integers consist of all positive and negative whole numbers and zero.\n\n$$\n…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…\n$$\n\n \n\nOf the given numbers, $1$ and $-2$ are integers, but $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151727 :answer-field/correct 17592186151731 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078507 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/id #uuid "c03bfbc1-ac68-5596-a4f4-f714ecc885a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-101757" :question/problem "What are the like terms in the expression $10x-18y-7z+10?$" :question/worked-solution "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(10x)+(-18y)+(-7z)+(10).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/id #uuid "df398605-069b-578f-992d-7e4d3a80a44a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" "answer-b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" "answer-8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" "answer-430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" "answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" :answer/id #uuid "cd60ad42-5e67-5777-adad-2ef5ec66220b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-18y$ and $-7z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" :answer/id #uuid "b03c765f-e75f-5dcf-809c-01376850ca45" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-18y$ and $10$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" :answer/id #uuid "8d5f42c9-e0cb-5e6f-a668-0a91b96a3f91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-7z$ and $10x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" :answer/id #uuid "430c59fb-0ec1-5a91-a924-97b3c1a01c01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10x$ and $10$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer/id #uuid "74649e04-5255-5f44-bde0-61194f6bfa86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No like terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171933 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/id #uuid "33724016-d9da-53c5-bcf3-d48acaf1fa22" :question/math-academy-id "q-85461" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $11\\,289\\,643$\n\nII. $13\\,298\\,784$\n\nIII. $215\\,153\\,238$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $11\\,289\\,643$ is not divisible by $2,$ so it is not divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- The number $13\\,298\\,784$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+3+2+9+8+7+8+4=42\n$$\n\nSo, $13\\,298\\,784$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $215\\,153\\,238$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n2+1+5+1+5+3+2+3+8=30\n$$\n\nSo, $215\\,153\\,238$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2693e54-d2f9-5e44-a62c-c85a8a82a915"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2693e54-d2f9-5e44-a62c-c85a8a82a915" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2693e54-d2f9-5e44-a62c-c85a8a82a915" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9af44677-9124-5bfd-b6ec-4ab308b7a5a2" "answer-2271ac3f-928c-59b8-9b16-901dbbb47dce" "answer-bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4" "answer-6e1bce80-8f6f-54f6-a118-9120fdf04361" "answer-185162bb-5aa3-5c3e-a43d-52c81ce56230"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9af44677-9124-5bfd-b6ec-4ab308b7a5a2" :answer/id #uuid "9af44677-9124-5bfd-b6ec-4ab308b7a5a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2271ac3f-928c-59b8-9b16-901dbbb47dce" :answer/id #uuid "2271ac3f-928c-59b8-9b16-901dbbb47dce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4" :answer/id #uuid "bbac0612-ed15-5839-94e6-475dabcd03b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e1bce80-8f6f-54f6-a118-9120fdf04361" :answer/id #uuid "6e1bce80-8f6f-54f6-a118-9120fdf04361" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-185162bb-5aa3-5c3e-a43d-52c81ce56230" :answer/id #uuid "185162bb-5aa3-5c3e-a43d-52c81ce56230" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073880 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a55cec5a-6ff7-549a-82f5-76546ccf37c7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a55cec5a-6ff7-549a-82f5-76546ccf37c7" :question/id #uuid "a55cec5a-6ff7-549a-82f5-76546ccf37c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-92945" :question/problem "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nTo paint his car, Anthony mixes blue paint with thinner. ​He requires $\\frac{3}{4}$ gallons of paint for every gallon of thinner. Therefore, the mixture has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ gallons of paint to $\\boxed{}$ gallons of thinner." :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{3}{4}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n3:4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mixture has a ratio of $3$ gallons of paint to $4$ gallons of thinner." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34a6e6c6-0e15-53b6-808a-63020a7889ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34a6e6c6-0e15-53b6-808a-63020a7889ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "34a6e6c6-0e15-53b6-808a-63020a7889ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f05742c-c5dd-55fd-82a0-9d57aea45582" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8f05742c-c5dd-55fd-82a0-9d57aea45582" "answer-3ea22cec-3976-5306-b057-80fe9b5fca34" "answer-7fb8aa12-476f-54d9-a946-3a656640cd8d" "answer-81318e94-fe4f-503d-9fe9-cea67c21da42" "answer-d182b9fc-285a-5a5a-a274-975a40cad8f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f05742c-c5dd-55fd-82a0-9d57aea45582" :answer/id #uuid "8f05742c-c5dd-55fd-82a0-9d57aea45582" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ea22cec-3976-5306-b057-80fe9b5fca34" :answer/id #uuid "3ea22cec-3976-5306-b057-80fe9b5fca34" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ and $7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fb8aa12-476f-54d9-a946-3a656640cd8d" :answer/id #uuid "7fb8aa12-476f-54d9-a946-3a656640cd8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ an